# CTF-01 actual OriginalDataQA source

Held source only. No reader/dependency has been imported or executed here, and no
actual Native result or binary payload was opened. Root supplies the future real
artifact references and explicitly approves the main source SHA before execution.
This is the required factual Original data review, not another SourceQA stage.

`review_data.py` authenticates exact frozen six-file identities, the real full
freeze stdout/recorder, seven Native source bindings, all 45 inherited input
guards, actual build preservation metadata and the independent PE evidence.
The compile recorder validates the actual compile; it is not claimed to have
authored Root's build metadata. Source guards are required; a clean worktree is
not required. The direct Native argv must be precisely helper/root/request/
admission/fresh-output. All preceding actual recorder intervals must precede it.
The reader binds recorder archives and streams, not Native executable bytes.

Runtime build metadata shape agreed with Root:
`ctf01-native-build.v1`, status `pass-actual-3TU-link-and-preservation`;
`helper_binary`, `linked_original`, `native_source_files` (seven ordered rows),
`configure_execution`, `compile_execution`, `derivation_execution`,
`validated_derivative` (metadata artifact), flat integer fields
previous_compile_rows661/current_compile_rows664/core_registered643/core_present631/core_absent12;
three actual preservation/provider flags required true.
The independent report is `ctf01-independent-build-PE-review.v1`, status
`pass-exact-retained-PE-runtime-and-actual-build-identity`, with `build`, the same
three binary/derivative bindings, `native_pe_source`, maps{original,derived,
comparison}, and `retained_runtime_exact:true`. Actual PE maps provide binary
identity and size; the reader never rehashes or parses either binary payload.
The actual recorded PE reader command and approved source identity are bound to
the supplied review through its genuine compact stdout {review,status}; the
stdout is not assumed to contain the full review JSON.

`shape.py` validates constructor/init/whole-call ledgers, actual stop masks,
ordered owner identity and snapshot shape, scalar class/bits/decimal consistency,
ordered diagnostic spans/log references, and the three actual callback records.
The actual after-member-input snapshot must retain the frozen literal member
bits, flags, dimensions, ordered LayerPoint membership and caller timestep bits.
This checks copied input provenance without evaluating CTF output arithmetic.
Only the actual copied active prefix is visited. Reached required operands must
exist. Unreached phases and uninvoked calls remain unavailable, with no invented
arrays, source outcomes, method counts or PASS. Nonfinite observed scalars retain
bits/class and availability. No classifier, sqrt, normalization, conversion,
resistance formula, expected array or numerical comparison is evaluated.

Complete valid exit2 output retains observed source/callback counts but fails
observer integrity and blocks Rust release. A failed process with no result has
unknown actual method counts and emits a factual failure review with exit1.
Malformed/incomplete payloads fail validation rather than fabricate observations.
Native fatal/exception/stopped source outcomes remain separate from OS/launch
failure and observation-integrity failure. An accepted DataQA0 releases only the
next Rust baseline step; it asserts no numerical or production/CTF02–10 PASS.

